==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stanga}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stangō}}. Compare {{cog|en|stang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtaŋə/}}
* {{rhymes|de|aŋə}}
* {{audio|de|De-Stange.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Stangen}}

# [[pole]]; [[bar]]; [[rod]]; [[post]] {{gloss|a long stick, usually round and of metal, but also of other material, especially when fixed somewhere}}
# a small straight [[glass]] for beer, especially [[Kölsch]]
# {{lb|de|of cigarettes}} [[carton]] {{gloss|lengthy box containing several packets}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly in {{m|de|eine Stange Geld}}}} a lot (of money); a [[packet]]
# {{lb|de|in {{m|de|von der Stange}} or compounds}} [[run-of-the-mill]], chiefly with clothes (referring to the poles on which clothes are presented in large fashion shops)
#: {{ux|de|'''Stangen'''kleidung ist mir nicht individuell genug.|I find '''run-of-the-mill''' garments lacking in individuality.}}

